From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Algorithms - BRepCheck_Edge::InContext copes with a face that has no
 surface and with an edge that has no 3D curve

BRepCheck_Edge::InContext checks an edge against a face. For a face it reads the face's surface
and goes on to use it, with two ways to reach a null handle:
 - The face has no surface. TopoDS faces without a geometry are legal (BRepCheck_Face reports
   BRepCheck_NoSurface for one), but InContext is also asked about each of the face's edges, and
   when the edge has a curve that is not a curve on a surface of this face it asks the null surface
   for its DynamicType (`Su->DynamicType()`), or transforms it (`Su->Transformed`).
 - The edge has no 3D curve and its reference curve is a curve on a surface. Minimum then sets
   myCref to that curve on a surface and myHCurve to its adaptor, which is not a GeomAdaptor_Curve.
   Because the loop over the edge's representations skips myCref itself, a planar face finds no
   other curve on its surface and projects "the 3D curve" onto the plane, through
   `occ::down_cast<GeomAdaptor_Curve>(myHCurve)->Curve()` on a null handle. The same edge on a
   face that is not a plane already reported BRepCheck_NoCurveOnSurface.

Both are uncatchable SIGSEGVs in BRepCheck_Analyzer, and the second needs no damaged file: a box
face whose edge loses its 3D curve (`BRep_Builder::UpdateEdge(E, Handle(Geom_Curve)(), tol)`)
faults. The readers return such shapes from a file that names a surface or a 3D curve the file
does not hold (`BRepTools_ShapeSet` and `BinTools_ShapeReader` skip a reference outside its table,
as patch 0074 records), which is how 2,208 of the 99,620 text count cases of Scripts/repro/3494
returned a shape and then faulted in `InContext`.

A face without a surface reports BRepCheck_NoCurveOnSurface for its edge and stops, and a planar
face whose reference is a curve on a surface reports the same as a face that is not a plane. Both
shapes are invalid, as they were whenever they did not fault, and now say so.

Tracked as SecondMouseAU/OCCTSwift#3490, the structurally inconsistent shape that BRepCheck
faults on.

---
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Edge.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Edge.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Edge.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKTopAlgo/BRepCheck/BRepCheck_Edge.cxx
@@ -338,6 +338,12 @@ void BRepCheck_Edge::InContext(const TopoDS_Shape& S)
         TopLoc_Location                  LE    = myShape.Location() * myCref->Location();
         const gp_Trsf&                   Etrsf = LE.Transformation();
         bool                             pcurvefound = false;
+        // a face without a surface has no curve on it to check; BRepCheck_Face reports the surface
+        if (Su.IsNull())
+        {
+          BRepCheck::Add(lst, BRepCheck_NoCurveOnSurface);
+          return;
+        }
 
         NCollection_List<occ::handle<BRep_CurveRepresentation>>::Iterator itcr(TE->Curves());
         constexpr double eps           = Precision::PConfusion();
@@ -470,8 +476,10 @@ void BRepCheck_Edge::InContext(const TopoDS_Shape& S)
           {
             P = occ::down_cast<Geom_Plane>(Su);
           }
-          if (P.IsNull())
-          { // not a plane
+          // not a plane, or a plane and the reference is itself a curve on a surface, so there is
+          // no 3D curve to project onto it
+          if (P.IsNull() || occ::down_cast<GeomAdaptor_Curve>(myHCurve).IsNull())
+          {
             BRepCheck::Add(lst, BRepCheck_NoCurveOnSurface);
           }
           else
